    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12396" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēbĭtrix</span></b> ,
			īcis, f.
		debitor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a female debtor</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					16, 1, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fisci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					49, 14, 47</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium delictorum debitrix anima est,</span>”
				<i>the guilty cause</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 35</span></i>
			.</div>
